# ${SRC_DIR}/features/

Feature folders for ${PROJECT_NAME}. Each feature owns its own components, hooks, services, and types.

## The strict 4-subfolder rule

Every feature has **exactly** these four subfolders:

| Subfolder | What lives here | Naming suffix |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `components/` | React components for the feature | `*.tsx` |
| `hooks/` | React Query hooks + plain hooks for the feature | `use*.ts` |
| `services/` | Network calls + business logic | `*.service.ts` |
| `types/` | Types and interfaces local to the feature | `*.types.ts` |

No file lives at the feature root — the only top-level file inside a feature folder is its own `README.md`.

## Examples

- [`health/`](health/) — working tiny example that calls `/healthz`. Stays minimal on purpose; do NOT grow it into an auth/DB demo.
